  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Capacity Development Partnership Fund Phase III (CDPF)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Cambodia):  .USAID/Cambodia, in partnership with other donors, builds the capacity of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports through the Capacity Development Partnership Fund (CDPF). CDPF is a multi-donor partnership managed by UNICEF to strengthen the Cambodian education sector to ensure that children increasingly receive quality, inclusive, and equitable education in more conducive learning environments. CDPF promotes better quality teaching and learning by: 1) building a system of Continuous Professional Development (CPD) for teachers to enhance their access to quality and relevant professional training to build their skills and competencies; 2) implementing school-based mentoring approaches for teachers, as part of a broader CPD framework and system; 3) assisting teachers to use positive discipline methodologies to promote student learning and to reduce violence in schools; 4) strengthening school-based management to promote transparency and accountability at schools; 5) building education system resilience to COVID-19 and other unprecedented emergency situations; and 6) enhancing multilingual education and inclusion...This activity falls under the Administration&apos;s priority to end the COVID-19 pandemic, advance global health security, and mitigate development and humanitarian impacts as well as to champion equity and inclusion for all by leveraging partnership and resources for strengthening education systems and fostering inclusiveness, resilience and sustainability. The activity will contribute to USAID/Cambodia&apos;s CDCS 2020-2025 Development Objective 2, &quot;Health, education, and welfare of Cambodians improved through enhanced services.&quot; It will also contribute to USG Education Strategy&apos;s Objective 2, &quot;Expand Access to Quality Basic Education for All, Particularly Marginalized and Vulnerable Populations.&quot;.</narrative>
  </description>
